title: We can deport Gallax.
subtitle: He is a foreign citizen and a criminal, after all.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if judicial_reform < 2 : Unfortunately, the <span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span> judiciary will not cooperate. ?] [? if gallax_citizen : Gallax has already been made a citizen of the Commonwealth, in the run-up to the presidential election. ?] [? if not marcher_heartland : We cannot do this without the cooperation of the Heartland police, who are not currently in our control. ?]
view-if: royalist_urgency >= 3 and gallax_deported = 0 and chancellor != "Goodryke" and chancellor != "Staal" and investigate_far_right >= 2
choose-if: judicial_reform >= 2 and not gallax_citizen and marcher_heartland == 1

Is it really that simple? Won't his supporters react violently to this suggestion? And even if the deportation does succeed, won't he just re-enter the country, or perhaps organize from the Freehold? And, some people consider this to be an anti-democratic abuse of power, using the law in order to target a political opponent.

- @deport: Deport him!
- @no_deport: No, we must not.

@deport
go-to: deport_violence if loyalist_strength >= 200; deport_success if loyalist_strength < 200

@deport_violence

When the police approach, he is surrounded by his <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> guards, preventing him from being extricated! We can attempt to force a confrontation, but that may have negative consequences. The the Banners may also attempt to draw off the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span>.

- @force_approach: Force the approach!
- @no_deport: Cancel the deportation.

@force_approach
on-arrival: {!
var total_allied_strength = Q.banner_strength*Q.banner_militancy + Q.heartland_police_strength*Q.heartland_police_militancy*Q.heartland_police_loyalty;
var enemy_strength = Q.loyalist_strength*Q.loyalist_militancy;
console.log('Deporting Gallax - force approach');
console.log(total_allied_strength, enemy_strength);

if (total_allied_strength > enemy_strength) {
    Q.deportation_success = 1;
} else {
    Q.deportation_success = 0;
}
!}
go-to: force_fail if deportation_success == 0; force_success if deportation_success = 1

@force_fail
on-arrival: loyalist_strength += 50; commons_royalist += 5; disfavored_royalist += 5; burgher_royalist += 5; guild_royalist += 5; landed_royalist += 5; coup_progress += 3; pro_republic -= 5

Unfortunately, our forces fail to dislodge the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> from their positions surrounding Gallax. He is seen as both a strong and powerful leader and a victim, further reinforcing his image. The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> are left stronger than ever.

@force_success
on-arrival: gallax_deported = 1; loyalist_strength = loyalist_strength/2; commons_royalist *= 0.7; burgher_royalist *= 0.7; guild_royalist *= 0.7; landed_royalist *= 0.7; disfavored_royalist *= 0.7; interior_goal_heartland -= 1 if not loyalist_banned; loyalist_banned = 1; coup_progress -= 2; royalist_leader = "Standerton"; royalist_chancellor = "Gorrick"; pro_republic += 10
achievement: deport_hitler

The confrontation ends with the police and the Banners prevailing, capturing Gallax so he can be deported! This is a sign of weakness, and his physical distance makes organizing difficult, impeding the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> effort to win more votes.

In Gallax's absence, Alden Standerton has become the temporary leader of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> party, with substantial influence from Ulric Gorrick.

@deport_success
on-arrival: gallax_deported = 1; loyalist_strength = loyalist_strength/2; commons_royalist *= 0.7; burgher_royalist *= 0.7; guild_royalist *= 0.7; landed_royalist *= 0.7; disfavored_royalist *= 0.7; interior_goal_heartland -= 1 if not loyalist_banned; loyalist_banned = 1; coup_progress -= 2; royalist_leader = "Standerton"; royalist_chancellor = "Gorrick"; pro_republic += 10
achievement: deport_hitler

Somehow, the plan worked! There was minimal resistance to Gallax's deportation. This is a sign of weakness, and his physical distance makes organizing difficult, impeding the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> effort to win more votes.

In Gallax's absence, Alden Standerton has become the temporary leader of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> party, with substantial influence from Ulric Gorrick.

@no_deport
go-to: root

We will not be deporting Gallax.
